main.go:283-289: ListenAndServe runs in a goroutine and its error is only logged -- into the redirected log file in window mode -- while the next statement unconditionally reports that the MCP server is running on the URL. Trigger: a second unreagent instance, or anything else already on the configured port. The agent's tool calls are then routed to the other instance's editor. A malformed mcp.address behaves the same, and it survives load because that field is not substituted (see the placeholder ticket). Acceptance: net.Listen up front and return the error from run().
